    "updated_at": "2016-08-09T21:22:50Z",
    "body": "> No normative change is intended here, just clarifying the existing semantics in the spec.\n\nOK. Got it.\n\nThere is an actual implication of `hgroup` being a heading itself. Had to go and check my implementation and I think I got it right - when the outline is created with links, I add the anchor to the `hgroup` and not to the `h?` inside of it.\n\nWould it make sense to slightly reword the first part of the note to something like \"If the element being entered is an <code>hgroup</code> element, then it is a multi-level heading for the <var>current section</var>\"? i.e. put more emphasis that the `hgroup` itself is a heading.\n",
